"provider, fresh nonce, aggregate wallet cap and held funds; unauthorized / over budget | `ServiceLaneFunded` |\\n| `redeem_service(lane, voucher)` | lane's provider, directly or through an authorized proxy dispatching as the provider; fixed payee | signature/domain/range; strictly increasing sequence and nondecreasing counters; exact pinned-tariff amount above paid and within budget; Closing requires known finalized height \u2264 deadline regardless of signing time; only the cumulative delta; replay / overclaim / expired claim / unknown clock | `ServicePaid` |\\n| `close_service_lane(lane)` / `finalize_service_lane(lane)` | payer to close; any caller to finalize | fixed boundary at close inclusion or earlier reservation end; pinned deadline = boundary + claim window; preserve slot and escrow; refund exactly remaining escrow only with known finalized height > deadline; unauthorized / claims pending / unknown clock | `ServiceLaneClosing` / `ServiceLaneClosed` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Appendix H \u2014 Conformance & Implementation-Status Matrix\\n\\nThe single home for **implementation status** (kept out of the normative body, \u00a70). Status legend:\\n`LIVE` implemented \u00b7 `PARTIAL` partly implemented \u00b7 `PLANNED` designed, not wired \u00b7 `GAP`\\nunhandled/unspecified \u00b7 `OOS` out of protocol scope by design. This appendix is informative and tracks\\nthe codebase; the normative *requirement* is always the cited section.\\n\\n### H.1 Core protocol\\n\\n| Requirement / mechanism | \u00a7 | Status |\\n|-------------------------|---|--------|\\n| Public claim evidence | \u00a70 | PENDING: private Lean/Quint bundle reproduced under named hypotheses; public source/run bundle awaits a software-license grant; implementation refinement and empirical evidence remain open |\\n| BABE authoring + AlephBFT finality (1 s blocks) | \u00a72 | LIVE |\\n| Per-rotation VRF committee sampling | \u00a72.3, \u00a715.4 | LIVE draw; \u2264100 pool returns all; stake-only fallback drops recency whenever no active validator clears both the stake floor and recency (including every recent-work validator below the floor); capture/min-size proof GAP (E.42) |\\n| Verification-liveness committee gate (R2.4, R15.4c) | \u00a72.3, \u00a715.4 | PLANNED: recency still written from prover credit only (`ValidatorWorkRecorder` credits the submitter of a verified PoUI proof); no protocol-issued duties; no attestation client (E.52). Until wired, only an account that also mines passes recency, paying the miner capacity bond and credit cap (\u00a72.4), so the \u00a72.3 stake-only committee cost does not yet hold |\\n| Committee Sybil capital: self-stake vs backing | \u00a72.3, \u00a715.2 | PARTIAL: D-0530 prohibits third-party delegated staking (self-stake only), while the runtime still exposes legacy `delegate` / `sponsor_validator` paths pending cleanup. The committee gate compares `total_stake` (self + delegated + sponsored) with `effective_minimum_stake()`. That backing is now distinct capital: every miner-staking and validators admission requires the account's balance to cover all of its staking positions, and one shared stake-ledger freeze holds their sum, because freezes overlap rather than add. An account that already owed more than it held before that freeze stays fully frozen but under-backed until topped up. GAP: self-stake is floor-checked at `register`/`rejoin` and from the recorded bond at queue promotion; `MinSelfStakeRatio` is checked only when backing is added, and a liveness slash charges self-stake first while `un_jail` restores without a re-check except on D-0528-enabled builds, where it restores the bonded floor like `rejoin` (E.42) |\\n| Queued validator self-stake top-up | \u00a715.2, \u00a715.5 | GAP: `register` bonds exactly the effective minimum; extra free balance does not increase recorded self-stake. `rejoin` tops up only extended-downtime-kicked validators, so a queued candidate below a raised floor remains deferred until the floor falls or registration is replaced. Backing admission is bounded by recorded self-stake |\\n| Sponsored registration bonds (R6.1a) | \u00a76.1, \u00a715.2 | PARTIAL: source landed; on by build feature in the devnet (`volta`) and `testnet` runtimes (the feature alone is a compile error; CI checks the default-feature mainnet node reports it off); the sponsor's own fungible holds can still overlap its frozen principal (E.32) |\\n| Three safety sub-proofs | \u00a72.3 | GAP: seat-capture/undersized/bootstrap bridge open (E.42) |\\n| GHOSTDAG/PoW fork removed; GRANDPA removed | \u00a72 | LIVE |\\n\\n### H.2 Verification (\u00a73)\\n\\n| Requirement / mechanism | Status |\\n|-------------------------|--------|\\n| TEE attestation (DCAP/dstack), quote \u2192 `report_data` | LIVE (on-TDX e2e pending) |\\n| Measured `model_hash` \u2014 reproducible packer + registry-root gate + verifier RTMR3 parse | LIVE (CVM RTMR3 extension PLANNED) |\\n| Output binding (`output_hash`) + decode-policy binding | LIVE |\\n| TOPLOC Tier 2 (commitment required; end-to-end error bound open) | PARTIAL |\\n| Tier 3 re-execution / session dispute game | PARTIAL |\\n| Re-execution checker lane (R3.5d: checkers re-run, validators verify + co-sign) | PLANNED: shipped checker re-prefills inside the validator watchtower (E.53) |\\n| Tier 4 validator BFT quorum crediting | LIVE |\\n| Canonical wire/rejection profile + public Rust/TS/Python vectors | PARTIAL: formats/vectors LIVE; task-domain producer/validator enforcement and legacy receipt resume profile open (E.51) |\\n| TEE-optional reframe (TEE-independent floor; TEE = optional HARD tier) | DECIDED |\\n| Non-TEE (SOFT) settlement lane end-to-end | PARTIAL: SOFT calibration entry, non-attested model onboarding (`flop model onboard --soft`) and persistent non-TEE session signing keys landed; miner registration still requires a `TeeType`; spot-check rate, demand-floor exclusion and checker-lane disputes open |\\n\\n### H.3 Metering, sizing, DA (\u00a74\u2013\u00a75)\\n\\n| Requirement / mechanism | Status |\\n|-------------------------|--------|\\n| Reference-work `G_n` accounting engine (MoE + attention, KAT-pinned) | LIVE |\\n| Runtime emission of reference-work `g_n` into `report_data` | LIVE |\\n| Reject-only throughput tripwire | LIVE |\\n| Per-GPU MLPerf ceiling / under-report floor | PARTIAL |\\n| `G_n` integer unit taxonomy | LIVE: wire/settlement checks; the reference meter, RISC0 audit guest and SDKs reject out-of-width values instead of clamping |\\n| Cache-aware settlement discount | PLANNED |\\n| Sovereign DA \u2014 on-chain protocol + `DataRef` plumbing | LIVE |\\n| DA availability, anti-grinding, repair and retention budget | GAP \u2014 PENDING E.47 |\\n| DA audits outstanding at lease withdrawal or prune | GAP \u2014 PENDING E.47 |\\n| Sovereign DA \u2014 off-chain validator service (RS encode/serve/audit) | PARTIAL |\\n| Protocol DA duty; serve-or-slash; leased weights + refundable deposit (\u00a75.3) | LIVE |\\n| Paid encrypted agent objects, memory heads, capabilities, storage escrow, and retrieval vouchers (\u00a75.4) | PARTIAL on development networks only (R5.4q): the `paid-storage` pallet runs at runtime index 108 behind the devnet-only `paid-storage-unratified` feature, with the da-validator paid data plane and the TypeScript SDK; rent is released without a custody audit (`UnratifiedNoAudit`). Production ACTIVATION BLOCKED by E.54/E.47 |\\n| Paid-storage Lean accounting, authority, and historical-liability invariants (\u00a75.4) | PARTIAL: unbounded draft contracts and countermodels; slot/tranche rounding ratified by D-0524; full composition and runtime conformance PENDING |\\n| Paid-storage Quint lifecycle, adversary, and conformance models (\u00a75.4) | PARTIAL: lifecycle, authority, admission, rent and lane models run in CI (sampled invariants, not exhaustive); runtime refinement PENDING |\\n| Paid-storage agent/validator market and solvency simulation (\u00a75.4) | PARTIAL: TypeScript and Julia storage-market and validator-solvency models with seeded scenario results; not a launch tariff (tariff ratification #1565) |\\n| Reorg-safe indexer serving (finalized prefix) | PARTIAL |\\n\\n### H.4 Primitives, calibration, vesting, emission (\u00a76\u2013\u00a79)\\n\\n| Requirement / mechanism | Status |\\n|-------------------------|--------|\\n| balances/multisig/proxy/staking/vesting (operator delegation deprecated per D-0530) | LIVE |\\n| Capacity-proportional miner self-stake (linear, no cap) | LIVE (value provisional) |\\n| Declarative spend-condition layer; N-party escrow; capabilities | PARTIAL |\\n| Agent session keys + caps + circuit breaker | LIVE (R6.2c latch survives the tripping call; an enclosing atomic batch that fails later still rolls it back) |\\n| 10-minute benchmark entry (SOFT/HARD), deposit-first | LIVE |\\n| Multi-GPU `(SKU,count)` inventory + aggregate HARD ceiling | LIVE |\\n| Seven-day lease; restart/expiry renewal supervisor | LIVE |\\n| Timed issuer-selected calibration packs | LIVE |\\n| Legacy three-phase dyno | REMOVED |\\n| Statistical rolling degradation/downshift | PLANNED |\\n| Drift: EWMA/control charts + MLPerf ceiling | PLANNED |\\n| Performance-locked vesting `R_p\u00b2` + blackout | LIVE (Root `force_create_grant` bypasses the \u00a77 baseline) |\\n| Era-T conversion snapshot and per-cohort allocation (\u00a78.2) | PARTIAL (cohort pools enforced; completed-job and active-day weights removed, as R8.4 requires; score caps and aggregation open in E.38) |\\n| Genesis airdrop funding and grants (\u00a78.2) | PARTIAL (genesis bridge absent; existing grant calls mint) |\\n| Airdrop claims, unlock schedule, and locked compute spend (\u00a78.2 R8.7, R8.8) | PARTIAL (claims use finality and locked compute spend is wired; the pallet still vests every tier linearly with the retired miner performance adjustment and `update_miner_performance`, and lets any tier spend locked principal; no genesis quarter, earn-to-unlock credit, or Validator freeze and daily release; no Agent spend credit or spend cap, and compute-channel refunds re-freeze up to the locked principal a channel drew and revert the close if they cannot. Miner self-stake over a still-frozen grant rides on overlapping `AirdropVesting` and `MinerSelfStake` freezes, but `miner-slashing` and `validators` lower only their own stake freeze before transferring proceeds, so a slash that reaches frozen grant principal fails today) |\\n| Ghost Tasks: encrypted issuance + known-answer correctness canary | LIVE |\\n| Emission/halving/subsidy/committee premium | LIVE |\\n| Reward liquidity on issue (\u00a79.1 R9.13) | LIVE (validator earnings and sponsored-stake payouts are liquid, like the miner leg and the Labs/Foundation subsidy; earnings do not grow stake or its freeze. The agent and staker legs accrue in pool accounts until E.40 ratifies their distribution. The +9%/year baseline, capped at 1% of issuance, and `max(baseline, ValueCoupledStakeFloor)` eligibility floor remain independent: unchanged stake can fall below the growing floor) |\\n| Tx-fee split (0% burn / 100% author, R9.6) | LIVE |\\n| Survival governor (both dampers) | PARTIAL (default OFF) |\\n\\n### H.5 HTLC, invariants, sessions, governance, validators (\u00a710\u2013\u00a715)\\n\\n| Requirement / mechanism | Status |\\n|-------------------------|--------|\\n| FLOP-leg HTLC create/redeem/refund; cross-chain pair profiles | LIVE local mechanics; all implemented pair directions target-only \u2014 conformance PENDING E.48 |\\n| Finality-safe FLOP refund; permissioned FLOP relayer gate | LIVE local mechanics; pair-level binding/finality PENDING E.48 |\\n| Agent-economics invariants (INV-02, INV-S01 session nonce, INV-M06 payout atomicity) | LIVE for INV-02, INV-S01 and INV-M06; `fail_task` removed with the per-task path |\\n| INV-S03 pallet allowlist; INV-S05 immediate revocation | LIVE: direct calls checked; known runtime dispatch wrappers rejected for every session; revocation immediate |\\n| Session `G_n` plausibility gate + authenticated submitted-turn sum | LIVE arithmetic/authentication; execution guarantee GAP (E.43/E.44) |\\n| Current-profile channel payment without public work credit (R11.2b) | LIVE payment-only; future audited credit and historical recovery OPEN (E.44) |\\n| Sessions: cooperative path has 2 primary inclusions; variable turn/path/evidence cost; reserved capacity; 85/15 fee split | LIVE mechanics; 85/15 fee split RATIFIED (D-0525, #2702); capacity mechanism PENDING; serialized bytes PARTIAL; withdrawal PROPOSED (ratification pending); benchmark/network GAP (E.44/E.46) |\\n| Terminal DA-loss settlement (R13.0c / V4) | GAP: receipt payout in code conflicts with D-0430 full-refund rule; a missing tariff now rejects (`SettlementTariffMissing`) except for a pre-v2 legacy channel, which the migration flag converts once |\\n| Failed/early-close three-way split (`\u03c6`) | LIVE |\\n| Dispute standing (agent + validators) | LIVE |\\n| Recursive dispute bisection beyond single turn | LIVE: on-chain midpoint rounds over complete power-of-two settled bundles; other bundles use single-turn `open_dispute` |\\n| Market-actor collusion detector + mechanism perturbation (R12.3) | PARTIAL: off-chain detector and dry-run perturbation canary LIVE; mechanism action open |\\n| Attestation-outage scoped pause (R13.0e / O1) | PLANNED: designed, not built |\\n| Session re-attestation cadence + max-duration extension | PLANNED |\\n| Per-task path removal | LIVE |\\n| OpenGov + `protocol_upgrade` (Root) track; Foundation submit gate; de-sudo | LIVE (de-sudo genesis-time) |\\n| Validator onboarding/duties/rotation | LIVE (stake-ordering PARTIAL; runtime minimum-set guard and bounded ejection implemented; floor/bootstrap/batch policy PENDING E.56/E.42) |\\n| Validator slashing table | LIVE (correlated equivocation curve PARTIAL) |\\n| V6 censorship (FOCIL); V8 ghost-task accountability; O3 attestation reputation; P3 provenance; A8 account recovery | PLANNED |\\n| Committee-sampling composition machine-check; PQ crypto | PARTIAL/OOS: committee gate predicate proved, including the bootstrap fallback; seat-capture composition PLANNED (E.42); quantum out of scope |\\n| Session capacity units (R11.2) | PARTIAL: source landed (elapsed-time bound; pre-open finality lag excluded); runtime qualification and deployment pending; the value-audit planner is SDK-only, with no production caller yet |\\n\\n**Regenerating the evidence-coverage matrix.** The per-section research/Lean/Quint/Julia backing is\\ngenerated separately into [`yellowpaper-coverage.md`](yellowpaper-coverage.md) via\\n`just yellowpaper-regen`.\\n\\n**Per-requirement attribution.** A finer, requirement-level map (each `R-id` \u2192 its Lean theorem / Quint\\ninvariant / Rust code path) is kept in the companion index\\n[`yellowpaper-attribution.md`](yellowpaper-attribution.md). It is non-normative and lives outside the\\nspec by design \u2014 it exposes proof-artifact and code-path detail the normative body omits.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Appendix I \u2014 Runtime Composition\\n\\nThe `construct_runtime!` inventory (source: `pallets/runtime/zkverify/src/lib.rs`). **Pallet indices are\\nconsensus- and encoding-critical:** they prefix every dispatch and storage key, so an index change is a\\nbreaking runtime upgrade requiring a migration (\u00a714.1). Indices are stable identifiers, not a sequence \u2014\\ngaps are intentional (removed pallets are not reused). This appendix is normative for the index values.\\n\\n**Core / system**\\n\\n| Idx | Pallet | Role |\\n|----:|--------|------|\\n| 0 | `frame_system` | base runtime |\\n| 1 \u00b7 2 | `scheduler` \u00b7 `preimage` | governance enactment / timelock / large-call storage (\u00a714) |\\n| 3 | `timestamp` | block time |\\n| 4 | `balances` | token accounts; existential deposit (\u00a76.5) |\\n| 5 | `transaction_payment` | fee model (\u00a74.2, \u00a79) |\\n\\n**Consensus**\\n\\n| Idx | Pallet | Role |\\n|----:|--------|------|\\n| 6 | `authorship` | block author note |\\n| 8 \u00b7 9 | `offences` \u00b7 `session_historical` | offence reports / historical session proofs (slashing, \u00a711) |\\n| 10 \u00b7 11 \u00b7 13 | `babe` \u00b7 `session` \u00b7 `authority_discovery` | BABE authoring; session keys; peer discovery (\u00a72) |\\n| 104 | `aleph` | AlephBFT committee snapshot + `LastFinalized` \u2192 `FinalizedPrefix` (\u00a72, \u00a715.4) |\\n\\n*Removed (D-0408): `pallet_staking` (was 7) and `bags_list` (was 19) \u2014 `validators` (96) is the sole\\nauthority source (\u00a76.1).*\\n\\n**Governance & utility**\\n\\n| Idx | Pallet | Role |\\n|----:|--------|------|\\n| 14 | `treasury` | on-chain treasury (\u00a714) |\\n| 15 \u00b7 16 \u00b7 17 | `conviction_voting` \u00b7 `referenda` \u00b7 `custom_origins` | OpenGov (\u00a714.1\u2013\u00a714.2) |\\n| 25 \u00b7 26 | `bounties` \u00b7 `child_bounties` | treasury bounties |\\n| 30\u201333 | `utility` \u00b7 `multisig` \u00b7 `proxy` \u00b7 `identity` | batching; multisig (\u00a76.1); proxy delegation (\u00a76.1); identity |\\n| 99 \u00b7 105 | `emergency_override` \u00b7 `emergency_pause` | break-glass + circuit breaker (\u00a714.1 R14.6) |\\n\\n**Bootstrap (removed at mainnet genesis handoff)**\\n\\n| Idx | Pallet | Role |\\n|----:|--------|------|\\n| 50 | `sudo` | bootstrap Root; **neutered + removed** at de-sudo (\u00a714.1 R14.3/R14.5) |\\n| 51 | `vesting` | generic vesting; removable once vesting completes |\\n\\n**FLOP protocol**\\n\\n| Idx | Pallet | Role \u00b7 spec \u00a7 |\\n|----:|--------|---------------|\\n| 81 | `aggregate` | verified-statement Merkle roots for cross-chain dispatch (\u00a73.6) |\\n| 83 \u00b7 84 | `token_claim` \u00b7 `crl` | airdrop claims \u00b7 certificate revocation |\\n| 85 | `has_station` | HTLC + predicate escrow (\u00a710) |\\n| 86 | `flop_poui` | PoUI proof verification, validator attestation, `flop_meter` (\u00a73.6, \u00a74) |\\n| 87 | `hw_calibration` | aggregate host calibration cap + renewable lease (\u00a77) |\\n| 88 \u00b7 91 | `work_vesting` \u00b7 `airdrop_vesting` | `R_p\u00b2` performance vesting (\u00a78) \u00b7 airdrop vesting (\u00a78.2) |\\n| 89 | `synthetic_tasks` | Ghost Tasks \u2014 liveness + correctness canary (\u00a78.1) |\\n| 90 | `attest` | shared attestation-profile registry (\u00a73.6) |\\n| 92 \u00b7 93 | `block_rewards` \u00b7 `flop_subsidy` | emission split (\u00a79) \u00b7 era-0 Labs/Foundation subsidy (\u00a79) |\\n| 94 \u00b7 95 \u00b7 106 | `session_keys` \u00b7 `agent_wallet` \u00b7 `agent_identity` | agent delegation + caps + circuit breaker (\u00a76.2) |\\n| 96 \u00b7 97 \u00b7 98 \u00b7 100 | `validators` \u00b7 `miner_staking` \u00b7 `delegation_cap` \u00b7 `miner_slashing` | validator authority + rotation + slashing (\u00a715); miner self-stake + slashing (\u00a76.1, \u00a711; `delegation_cap` and `miner_staking::delegate` deprecated per D-0530) |\\n| 101 \u00b7 102 \u00b7 103 | `model_registry` \u00b7 `da_registry` \u00b7 `compute_channel` | measured roots + decode-policy pins (\u00a73.3); sovereign DA (\u00a75.3); sessions (\u00a712) |\\n| 107 | `metering_verifier` | metering-certificate verification (\u00a74, E.34) |\\n\\n**Settlement verifiers** (`160\u2013170`) \u2014 **zkVerify aggregation, not inference proofs** (\u00a73.6):\\n`common` (160), `groth16` (161), `risc0` (162), `ultraplonk` (163), `plonky2` (165), `fflonk` (166),\\n`sp1` (167), `ultrahonk` (168), `ezkl` (169), `tee` (170).\\n\",\"lastModified\":null},{\"source\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flop-labs/yellowpaper/5730f4b6cf56fa88bb93bbda272dc449b2f77b17/CHANGELOG.md\",\"status\":200,\"measuredAt\":\"2026-11-06T03:27:26.823Z\",\"body\":\"# Yellowpaper changelog\\n\\nThe initial public release is **0.5.0 (draft)**. No version has been published yet. Prepublication\\nedits are folded into the initial text.\\nAfter publication, use [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html) and\\n[Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), preserving released versions.\\n\\n## [Unreleased]\\n\\n### Changed\\n\\n- State in \u00a715.5 R15.5 that proven-fault slash proceeds at the active-set floor are confiscated and transferred to the Foundation (R9.10) rather than burned.\\n\\n- Propagate the zero-burn, operator self-stake-only, and off-chain referral rulings to the normative\\n  spec and canonical parameters (D-0529, D-0530, D-0531; #2792, #1945, #1358): set\\n  `tx_fee_burn_percent_live` (`BurnFees`) to 0% with 100% of live transaction fees and tips routed to\\n  the block author (\u00a79.1 R9.6, Appendix D, Appendix H); replace legacy \\\"full-burn\\\" slash terminology\\n  with 100% routing to `FLOPFoundationAccount` (\u00a711.3, \u00a713.2, \u00a715.7, Appendix A); prohibit third-party\\n  delegated staking into validators and miners, deprecate delegation extrinsics/caps and operator\\n  commissions (`miner_staking::delegate`, `max_delegators_per_miner`, `miner_commission_cap_percent`),\\n  and formalize the 5% duration-locked community staking pool across seven lock tiers without\\n  slashing risk (\u00a72.3, \u00a76.1, \u00a79.1 R9.12, \u00a711.3, \u00a715.2, E.32, E.40, G.3); and record that the\\n  800,000,000 FLOP `genesis_reserve` funds the off-chain explorer referral leaderboard and periodic\\n  lotteries in place of on-chain referral commissions (\u00a79.1 R9.4, E.38).\\n\\n- Let sponsors post an operator's whole registration bond on devnet and testnet (R6.1a; D-0528). The\\n  bond stays frozen in the sponsor account and is refunded only to the sponsor. It counts as miner or\\n  validator self-stake only on runtimes built with `sponsored_self_stake_enabled`. Narrow E.32 to its\\n  mainnet questions; index the new calls in G.3 and their status in H.1.\\n\\n- Reconcile normative contradictions surfaced by the 2026-10-13 mirror sync (#2648): align \u00a715.5,\\n  E.56 and H.5 with the implemented `validator_min_active_validators` = 4 removal/rotation floor and\\n  10% churn cap (#1727) while keeping the D-0507/D-0508/E.42 policy questions open; reconcile \u00a79.3\\n  R9.9, \u00a715.5 R15.5/R15.5b and Appendix G.3 on active-set entry paths (`rotate` promotion from\\n  `ValidatorQueue` vs direct `un_jail`/`rejoin` restoration under `validator_active_set_cap`, and\\n  rotation ejection thawing self-stake before re-registration); align \u00a79, R9.2, R9.3, Appendix A and\\n  Appendix D cumulative emission and subsidy totals with the runtime's `era(b) = \u230ab / H\u230b` boundary\\n  and unrewarded genesis block 0 (R9.7); define the +9%/yr validator stake baseline's annual\\n  `31,536,000`-block boundary, integer floor formula and 1%-of-`total_issuance` cap in \u00a715.2; update\\n  \u00a713.2 V11 and E.57 to compose `W` against R1.2a's multi-round bisection dispute lifetime (`8 d 20 h`);\\n  define Validator grant unlocked amount (`P \u2212 S`) and slashed-principal accounting `S` in \u00a78.2\\n  R8.7/R8.8; and clarify in \u00a711.2 R11.2b and \u00a78.2 R8.7 that settled-session airdrop unlock/spend\\n  credit is private payment-denominated vesting credit distinct from public `G_n` work credit.\\n\\n- Credit miner block rewards toward the Miner airdrop unlock (R8.7; D-0527, superseding D-0517\\n  item 1). A Miner grant now unlocks one FLOP per FLOP of the miner-leg block rewards minted to the\\n  grantee, counted once the distribution block is finalized, as well as per FLOP of its settled\\n  channel payouts after the dispute window. Other block-reward legs, the subsidy, transaction fees, refunds, penalties and\\n  bonds still earn nothing.\\n\\n- Mark INV-M06 payout atomicity LIVE in \u00a711.1 and H.5: channel settlement now reverts when the\\n  refund-penalty burn fails, as it already did for the miner and refund transfers.\\n\\n- Name RTMR3 as the only accepted measurement path for the model root (\u00a73.3 step 2), matching the\\n  step 3 verifier and D-0404.\\n\\n- Bring Appendix E/H status, trackers and code paths up to date with landed code; no protocol rule\\n  changes. Index the on-chain bisection dispute calls in G.1 and correct `open_dispute`'s arguments;\\n  mark multi-round bisection and `G_n` overflow rejection LIVE; record the development-network\\n  paid-storage pallet (rent released without audit), its CI-run Quint models and its simulation as\\n  PARTIAL; narrow E.9, E.32, E.41, E.46, E.47, E.51 and E.54 to what remains open; and replace\\n  enforcement paths for code removed with the per-task path in \u00a711.1 and H.5.\\n\\n- Specify Appendix D's chain inclusion-fee terms, align the shared-collateral example with its\\n  generated four-claim row, and list both work-vesting grant entry points in Appendix G.3.\\n\\n- Ratify slot/tranche position rent (D-0524, R5.4e/f, E.54, F.7, G.4): replacements retain\\n  historical earned rent, failed or forfeited deltas refund the payer, and new tariffs use separate\\n  funded tranches. Supersede independent provider ceilings; add seven executable balance vectors.\\n\\n- Describe implemented HTLC pair directions as target-only for initial publication (E.48).\\n  Preserve cross-leg late-claim, finality-stall and failed-payout counterexamples, qualify the local\\n  formal models, and add focused pallet/contract expiry-ordering tests and a reproducible pair gate.\\n\\n- Specify the Agent airdrop unlock as spend-to-unlock (R8.7, R8.8; D-0522). An Agent grant unlocks\\n  nothing at its start and has no end block; it unlocks one FLOP per three FLOP of its locked\\n  principal in the gross `payable` of settled sessions, once every fraud dispute raised in the window has\\n  resolved, and its locked compute spend is capped at three quarters of principal. Channel escrow\\n  drawn from locked principal goes to the `payable` first and is refunded first, back to the grant as frozen\\n  principal. E.38 no longer holds the Agent horizon.\\n\\n- Make current-profile channel settlements payment-only (\u00a711.2 R11.2b). Receipt claims no\\n  longer feed public work rewards or performance vesting, including unilateral/DA-void payout.\\n  Historical recovery and future audited credit remain open.\\n\\n- Tighten the Appendix F vector schema to require canonical fields, byte widths, integer ranges,\\n  case identities, and coverage. Wide integers use decimal strings so JSON consumers preserve\\n  their exact values; the public generator also checks duplicate identities.\\n- Protect Ephemeral DA blobs from pruning while any usage pin remains, matching Leased blobs\\n  (R5.3d; D-0521). Pins do not extend expiry or admit new usage after the retention deadline.\\n\\n- Replace \u00a78.2's Miner and Validator airdrop unlock (R8.7, R8.8; D-0517). A Miner grant is a quarter\\n  liquid at its start and unlocks the rest one FLOP per FLOP it receives as miner from settled\\n  sessions once their dispute window passes, with no end block (D-0527 adds miner block rewards), and\\n  the performance adjustment is retired. A Validator grant stays frozen until the first halving, then grants release one per day\\n  without unbonding; none releases until E.38 fixes the order. Only Agent grants may still spend\\n  locked principal on compute; a miner may bond its locked principal as its own self-stake.\\n- Make block rewards and the subsidy liquid on issue (R9.13; D-0518). The miner and validator legs and\\n  the Labs/Foundation subsidy are never auto-compounded, force-staked or vested, and agent-leg payouts\\n  are liquid once E.40 ratifies; validator earnings no longer auto-compound into locked stake, and E.39\\n  is closed.\\n\\n- Ratify \u00a78.2's grant-landing (R8.6) and claim and locked-spend (R8.8) rules as D-0515. D-0514\\n  had covered only R8.3\u2013R8.5 and R8.7; the requirement text is unchanged.\\n\\n- Repoint Appendix E blockers to live trackers and refresh Appendix H implementation grades for\\n  fee distribution, metering overflow, session-key invariants, and collusion monitoring.\\n\\n### Added\\n\\n- Specify paid-storage service lanes that close at a fixed boundary with\\n  a funding-pinned claim deadline on the finalized prefix. Only the lane's provider redeems, with\\n  strict sequence, counter and amount checks, including after reassignment. Otherwise-valid\\n  post-close signatures remain payable within the unspent budget until the deadline; finalization\\n  refunds only the remainder above it. Unknown finality rejects both operations. R5.4g, R5.4j,\\n  E.54, F.7 and G.4 carry the rule. E.54 constrains sequential entitlement-maturity and funded-request\\n  timing to fit that fixed deadline and requires an actual redeem-valid dispatch opportunity under\\n  permitted finality behavior before affected work can be enabled. Timing arithmetic alone does not\\n  establish it; the numerical window and production activation remain unratified.\\n\\n- Era-T conversion and airdrop vesting (\u00a78.2, R8.3\u2013R8.8; D-0514). Conversion draws only on the\\n  fixed genesis cohort pools. Agents are scored on settled compute-channel spend and miners on\\n  verified effective-FLOP; balance, stake, job count and active days carry no weight. Snapshot and\\n  evidence of record are fixed before genesis lock. Grants land as frozen genesis balances with\\n  linear vesting and finalized-head claims. The miner performance adjustment fails closed: without\\n  both performance inputs a Miner grant unlocks nothing before its end block. E.38 keeps score caps,\\n  the validator activity basis, the agent horizon and the remainder disposition open.\\n\\n- Development-network exception to the paid-storage activation gate (D-0512, R5.4q): a valueless\\n  devnet may run the \u00a75.4 extension ahead of E.54 only from a runtime built with a non-default,\\n  development-only flag, under an explicitly unratified profile with placeholder values kept out of\\n  the canonical parameters, with unaudited rent releases marked as such, and with no result citable\\n  as E.54/E.47 evidence. R5.4k now names R5.4q as its only exception; every other network is unchanged.\\n\\n- Paid encrypted agent memory/data storage specification (D-0506): fixed-term validator storage\\n  revenue, metered retrieval vouchers, scoped authority, versioned memory heads, and bounded\\n  audit/repair/refund obligations. Activation remains gated on E.54 economics/security calibration\\n  and E.47 availability evidence; protocol/model DA pricing is preserved. Distinguish client encryption\\n  from enforceable envelope validation, price setup separately from rent, and separate provider quotes\\n  from protocol limits and calibration inputs. Fund storage as take-or-pay capacity reservations:\\n  deletion frees bytes for reuse and refunds nothing, the remaining term is transferable, and rent\\n  rounds once per provider. Price by one epoch tariff (stake-weighted median of capacity-declaring\\n  validators, bounded step, under-supply tripwire) with protocol-random assignment among declarers.\\n  Keep the chain footprint flat: one reservation per payer, objects and ordinary memory heads in a\\n  provider-group manifest with quorum receipts and one checkpoint per provider per epoch, rent\\n  released per epoch without claims, setup and retrieval on one service lane per provider. Advance\\n "
